%------------------------------------------------------------------
\vspace{-2pt}
\subsection{Instruction Sensitivity: Counterfactual Perturbation}
\label{sec:cf_sensitivity}

\subsubsection{Instruction Sensitivity in Action-Producing VLAs}
\label{sec:cf_action}

We first evaluate counterfactual sensitivity in action-producing models using a shared action-space metric.
Across OpenVLA and TracVLA, instruction perturbations produce medium-to-large action divergence in all eight architecture-suite cells (Figure~\ref{fig:counterfactual_bar}).

\begin{wrapfigure}{r}{0.46\columnwidth}
\vspace{-8pt}
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.44\columnwidth]{figures/fig_counterfactual_bar.pdf}
\vspace{-4pt}
\caption{Counterfactual sensitivity across the architecture-suite matrix. (a)~Cohen's $d$ for four perturbation conditions (E=empty, W=wrong, S=shuffled, P=paraphrased); asterisks mark the top condition per cell; dashed line: large-effect threshold ($d = 0.8$). (b)~Cosine distance on hidden representations (different scale).}
\label{fig:counterfactual_bar}
\vspace{-8pt}
\end{wrapfigure}
Every perturbation condition yields $d = 0.45$--$1.52$ (Table~\ref{tab:cf_summary}; full per-condition rankings in Appendix Table~\ref{tab:counterfactual}).
The ``empty'' condition ranks first in 6 of 8 cells ($d = 1.17$--$1.52$); ``paraphrased'' ranks last in 7 of 8, indicating that VLAs encode instruction content beyond token-level matching.
TracVLA produces systematically higher effect sizes ($d = 0.97$--$1.52$) than OpenVLA ($0.45$--$1.21$).
Removing the instruction entirely often produces larger divergence than replacing it with a wrong task, consistent with instruction removal producing larger disruption than instruction substitution.

Two OpenVLA cells permit same-metric trained/reference comparison: on Spatial, training increases sensitivity (trained$-$reference difference: $+0.05$ to $+0.24$ across conditions); on Long-Horizon, the OXE-pretrained model exceeds the LIBERO-trained model ($d = 1.05$ vs.\ $0.57$), consistent with the general-purpose model maintaining broader instruction responsiveness.
\textbf{Instruction perturbation produces graded action divergence across all tested conditions, with effect sizes reflecting semantic distance.}

